<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"http:\/\/schema.org\/","@type":"Blog","headline":"Blizzard Watch","description":"","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com","blogPost":[{"@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"The Queue: And if you can believe it, it&#8217;s a Friday once again","description":"","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/18\/queue-can-believe-friday\/","sameAs":null,"datePublished":"2026-09-18T13:00:50-05:00","dateModified":"2026-09-18T09:19:13-05:00","mainEntityOfPage":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/18\/queue-can-believe-friday\/","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Phil Ulrich","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/author\/pulrich\/","description":"Phil Ulrich is a software developer from Cincinnati, an amateur game dev, a former raid leader (and current raider) for a WoW guild full of retired ex-raid-leaders, and sometimes even a writer. His time in World of Warcraft goes back to 2008, and he's really been hooked ever since. Outside of WoW and Diablo, Phil is also an avid console and PC RPG fan, and a tabletop RPG \"forever DM.\"","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/c344ac98b6234806094f53503105437c?s=96&d=mm&r=g","height":96,"width":96},"sameAs":["https:\/\/awaymessage.club\/@stoppableforce"]},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/#organization","name":"Blizzard Watch","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/11\/Twitter-Icon.jpg","width":600,"height":60}},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/wow_forever_hyjal_summit_exterior.jpg","width":696,"height":380},"keywords":"","commentCount":"0","comment":[]},{"@context":"https:\/\/schema.org\/","@type":"NewsArticle","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/18\/blizzard-watch-podcast-blizzcon-mega-episode\/"},"url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/18\/blizzard-watch-podcast-blizzcon-mega-episode\/","headline":"Blizzard Watch Podcast: The BlizzCon mega episode","datePublished":"2026-09-18T11:00:41-05:00","dateModified":"2026-09-18T00:22:45-05:00","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/#organization","name":"Blizzard Watch","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/11\/Twitter-Icon.jpg","width":600,"height":60}},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/BWP_599_header.jpg","width":696,"height":380},"articleSection":"Podcast","description":"BlizzCon just wrapped, and so there is so much to talk about we couldn't pack it all into an hour. We spent around an hour on WoW Forever, the new Classic+ that was rumored and is now coming to fruition with a sort-of alternate history. There was a lot of Midnight news","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Anna Bell","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/author\/abell\/","description":"Anna Bell -- and yes that is her real name -- has 2 kids, a degree in English literature, and has been playing video games as long as she can remember. In addition to Blizzard's game she's also into Farm Simulator esports, and romanced Alistair in Dragon Age.","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/02\/headshot1-96x96.jpg","height":96,"width":96},"sameAs":["https:\/\/bsky.app\/profile\/annabellreads.bsky.social","https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/user\/tamerliopleurodon"]}},{"@context":"https:\/\/schema.org\/","@type":"NewsArticle","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/17\/hands-last-call-arcantina-wow-tabletop-experience-exclusive-blizzcon\/"},"url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/17\/hands-last-call-arcantina-wow-tabletop-experience-exclusive-blizzcon\/","headline":"Hands-on with Last Call at the Arcantina, a WoW tabletop experience exclusive to BlizzCon","datePublished":"2026-09-17T15:00:00-05:00","dateModified":"2026-09-17T07:37:55-05:00","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/#organization","name":"Blizzard Watch","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/11\/Twitter-Icon.jpg","width":600,"height":60}},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/blizzcon_last_call_at_the_arcantina_art.jpg","width":696,"height":380},"articleSection":"BlizzCon","description":"One of the least advertised things on the BlizzCon 2026 map was a small area in the World of Warcraft section labeled \"Last Call at the Arcantina\". It turned out to be a hyper-short tabletop RPG experience for four players that was super fun, easy to jump into, and","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Eric O'Dea","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/author\/eodea\/","description":"Eric is a space nerd from Boston who has been playing video games since before he could read. His time in World of Warcraft stretches back to 2006, although most of his characters currently reside at the bottom of the Lakkari Tar Pits.","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/f739a8e14b8e05f907ebe0b0e6f5426b?s=96&d=mm&r=g","height":96,"width":96}}},{"@context":"https:\/\/schema.org\/","@type":"NewsArticle","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/17\/the-queue-game-last-forever\/"},"url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/17\/the-queue-game-last-forever\/","headline":"The Queue: Can a game really last forever?","datePublished":"2026-09-17T13:00:44-05:00","dateModified":"2026-09-17T04:17:46-05:00","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/#organization","name":"Blizzard Watch","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/11\/Twitter-Icon.jpg","width":600,"height":60}},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/wow-forever-dwarf-bear-trailer-still.jpg","width":696,"height":380},"articleSection":"The Queue","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Elizabeth Harper","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/author\/eharper\/","description":"In the real world, Elizabeth Harper started her writing career with a gig for WoW Insider in 2006. Now, she's spent the past 10 years writing and editing online content for tech, gaming, and entertainment. In the virtual world, she's been playing Warcraft since its earliest days and dabbles in Hearthstone, Heroes of the Storm, and Diablo.","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"http:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/03\/Elizabeth-Harper_avatar_1456859822-96x96.jpg","height":96,"width":96}}},{"@context":"https:\/\/schema.org\/","@type":"NewsArticle","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/17\/world-warcraft-forever-beta\/"},"url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/17\/world-warcraft-forever-beta\/","headline":"How to join the World of Warcraft: Forever beta, which starts on September 17 after the WoW Live Q&amp;A","datePublished":"2026-09-17T10:45:13-05:00","dateModified":"2026-09-17T10:57:58-05:00","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/#organization","name":"Blizzard Watch","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/11\/Twitter-Icon.jpg","width":600,"height":60}},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/bw-wow-forever-hyjal-zone.jpg","width":696,"height":380},"articleSection":"BlizzCon","description":"World of Warcraft: Forever is bringing new and expanded content and gameplay to Classic Azeroth when it launches worldwide on November 4, 2026 as part of your regular World of Warcraft subscription, no additional purchase necessary! If you just can't wait for November, there's an opportunity to get in early because the","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Nick Marino","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/author\/nmarino\/","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/916f5161d89d49fb90708359a448ad78?s=96&d=mm&r=g","height":96,"width":96}}},{"@context":"https:\/\/schema.org\/","@type":"NewsArticle","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/17\/tavern-watch-plays-fallout-episode-3-deals-dinosaurs-just-big-chickens\/"},"url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/17\/tavern-watch-plays-fallout-episode-3-deals-dinosaurs-just-big-chickens\/","headline":"Tavern Watch Plays Fallout, episode 3: Deals with dinosaurs (or just big chickens)","datePublished":"2026-09-17T10:00:47-05:00","dateModified":"2026-09-17T00:58:00-05:00","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/#organization","name":"Blizzard Watch","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/11\/Twitter-Icon.jpg","width":600,"height":60}},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/twp-fallout-ep3.jpg","width":696,"height":380},"articleSection":"Podcast","description":"Some days in the Wasteland, you accidentally stumble into a robot-operated dinosaur cloning facility, and then you have to make an ethical judgment on what to do with the lives of intelligent (and very polite) cloned dinosaurs and deathclaws. But being a resident of the Wasteland means being adaptable,","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Elizabeth Harper","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/author\/eharper\/","description":"In the real world, Elizabeth Harper started her writing career with a gig for WoW Insider in 2006. Now, she's spent the past 10 years writing and editing online content for tech, gaming, and entertainment. In the virtual world, she's been playing Warcraft since its earliest days and dabbles in Hearthstone, Heroes of the Storm, and Diablo.","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"http:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/03\/Elizabeth-Harper_avatar_1456859822-96x96.jpg","height":96,"width":96}}},{"@context":"https:\/\/schema.org\/","@type":"NewsArticle","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/17\/sights-feels-experiences-made-first-ever-blizzcon-worth-trip\/"},"url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/17\/sights-feels-experiences-made-first-ever-blizzcon-worth-trip\/","headline":"All the sights, feels, and experiences that made my first ever BlizzCon worth the trip","datePublished":"2026-09-17T09:00:55-05:00","dateModified":"2026-09-17T00:57:10-05:00","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/#organization","name":"Blizzard Watch","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/11\/Twitter-Icon.jpg","width":600,"height":60}},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/blizzcon_2026_sights_eric_selfies.jpeg","width":696,"height":380},"articleSection":"BlizzCon","description":"As you may have deduced by my recent run of BlizzCon coverage, last weekend was my first time attending the event in person. It was two full days of announcements, demos, nostalgia, and more cosplay than you can shake a Pepe staff at. More than anything, I wanted to","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Eric O'Dea","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/author\/eodea\/","description":"Eric is a space nerd from Boston who has been playing video games since before he could read. His time in World of Warcraft stretches back to 2006, although most of his characters currently reside at the bottom of the Lakkari Tar Pits.","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/f739a8e14b8e05f907ebe0b0e6f5426b?s=96&d=mm&r=g","height":96,"width":96}}},{"@context":"https:\/\/schema.org\/","@type":"NewsArticle","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/16\/can-expect-future-world-warcraft-classic-progression-servers\/"},"url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/16\/can-expect-future-world-warcraft-classic-progression-servers\/","headline":"What can we expect for the future of World of Warcraft Classic progression servers?","datePublished":"2026-09-16T19:00:08-05:00","dateModified":"2026-09-16T19:14:21-05:00","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/#organization","name":"Blizzard Watch","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/11\/Twitter-Icon.jpg","width":600,"height":60}},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/bw-dalaran-wotlk-classic-p2.png","width":696,"height":380},"articleSection":"WoW Classic","description":"Throughout BlizzCon 2026, we received plenty of information and news about the huge reveal of World of Warcraft: Forever, the roadmap for the rest World of Warcraft: Midnight, and even teasers for The Last Titan and Wrath of the Lich King Remix. Noticeably missing from the BlizzCon stage and schedule was anything","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Nick Marino","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/author\/nmarino\/","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/916f5161d89d49fb90708359a448ad78?s=96&d=mm&r=g","height":96,"width":96}}},{"@context":"https:\/\/schema.org\/","@type":"NewsArticle","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/16\/skyborne-classes-factions\/"},"url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/16\/skyborne-classes-factions\/","headline":"Who are the Skyborne? Which classes or faction can I choose if I want to play Skyborne in WoW: Forever?","datePublished":"2026-09-16T15:00:11-05:00","dateModified":"2026-09-16T11:46:14-05:00","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/#organization","name":"Blizzard Watch","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/11\/Twitter-Icon.jpg","width":600,"height":60}},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/WoW_Forever_Skyborne_Customization_01.png","width":696,"height":380},"articleSection":"BlizzCon","description":"With the release of World of Warcraft: Forever we will see a new race called the Skyborne, an elven race who were descended from Highborne elven exiles who made a pact with the Skywall wind elementals generations ago. Native to the Zephras Isle, in the alternative timeline that is","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Sara Hanson","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/author\/shanson\/","description":"I'm an older dilettante gamer who has been playing Blizzard games since Diablo first launched. I run a World of Warcraft guild that has been around since Vanilla. I am also a long time role player on both sides of the GM screen and boardgamer. I'm an advocate for representation and accessibility in game design. I have cats. They're warm and fluffy.","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/220812_sarahansonpfp-96x96.png","height":96,"width":96}}},{"@context":"https:\/\/schema.org\/","@type":"NewsArticle","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/16\/win-hearthstones-star-squad\/"},"url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/2026\/09\/16\/win-hearthstones-star-squad\/","headline":"The card you need to pick to win Hearthstone's All-Star Squad Tavern Brawl","datePublished":"2026-09-16T13:30:05-05:00","dateModified":"2026-09-16T13:34:44-05:00","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/#organization","name":"Blizzard Watch","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/11\/Twitter-Icon.jpg","width":600,"height":60}},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Hearthstone-tavern-brawl-all-star-squad.jpg","width":696,"height":380},"articleSection":"Hearthstone","description":"Hey now, you're an all-star, get your game on, go play. We've had Hearthstone Tavern Brawls that ask us to choose three cards to build our decks and Brawls that ask us to choose 2 cards to build our decks —but this week's All-Star Squad Tavern Brawl in Hearthstone is","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Ted Atchley","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/author\/ted\/","description":"Ted Atchley is a writer, gamer, and professional computer programmer. He’s been playing Blizzard games all the way back to the original Starcraft. He’s a fourteen year veteran of World of Warcraft with most of that time as a Paladin and has played Hearthstone since open Beta.\r\n\r\nHe lives in beautiful Charleston, SC with his wife and children. When not writing for Blizzard Watch or gaming, you’ll find him spending time with his family, working on his novel, and cheering on his beloved Carolina Panthers.  You can find more about his writing journey at tedatchley.com","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https:\/\/blizzardwatch.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/ted_square_100x100-96x96.png","height":96,"width":96}}}]}</script>

